  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "A change behind the leading six",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-roster-0"
      ],
      "text": "Domdolus Tolus closes seventh at 72.92 after the feed recorded a move from tenth at 71.67. That is an observed score event, not a verified net gain since yesterday’s close: this entry has no usable comparison at that boundary. The top six retain both their scores and places, with Tufa Labs first at 88.06, Yi-Chia Chen second at 84.72 and rabbithole third at 80.83. The change therefore reshuffles the chase behind the front group without changing who leads. ALbert RUehlman is eighth at an unchanged 72.64."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The climb below the gold line",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-22-1541-arc-2-aneesh-yash-gains-to-34th"
      ],
      "text": "codjjj reaches 33rd at 53.47, up six places and 3.61 points against the previous close. That is the largest verified net score gain among the edition’s selected candidates. The afternoon wire separately reported Aneesh & Yash reaching 34th at 53.33, a gain of 7.36 in its own rolling window. Those windows answer different questions and should not be combined into a daily ranking of gains. The closing gold line is 66.53, so codjjj remains well short of it. The wire’s suggestion that being below gold means being outside all medal places is too broad: this edition’s silver line is 32.64 and bronze line 31.81. All public medal bands are provisional."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A crowded top-hundred contest",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-22-0941-arc-2-ruslan-guseynov-into-top-fifty",
        "wire-2026-10-22-1241-arc-2-yuvraj-2-climbs-to-ninety-second",
        "wire-2026-10-22-1541-arc-2-giba-climbs-101-places-to-95th"
      ],
      "text": "tf climbs from 168th to 85th at 35.56 against the previous close; KaggleARC moves from 130th to 93rd at 34.86. Giba closes 96th at 34.44, up 100 places on the same comparison. The afternoon wire’s 95th-place Giba report was an earlier observation, so the score held while the rank slipped. Earlier wire reports also captured Ruslan Guseynov reaching 50th at 43.33 and Yuvraj #2 reaching 92nd at 34.86. Those are dated milestones from their wire snapshots, not closing ranks verified by this edition."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Three model reports, a separate scoreboard",
      "sourceIds": [
        "dispatch-2026-10-22-beam-1-model-report",
        "dispatch-2026-10-22-deepseek-flash-1017-model-report",
        "dispatch-2026-10-22-muse-spark-open-model-report"
      ],
      "text": "Today’s saved model reports examine ARC Prize’s semi-private evaluations: DeepSeek Flash 1017 reaches 78.1% on ARC-AGI-2 at maximum effort, Muse Spark Open reaches 57.5% at xhigh and Beam 1.0 reaches 23.5% at xhigh. These are model evaluations, separate from Kaggle team standings. The DeepSeek report flags incomplete dataset coverage at the high setting, so its effort curve cannot support a simple claim that more thinking hurt performance. The reports were checked October 22; the model release dates are earlier, and none establishes a new ARC-AGI-3 score."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Coverage",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Social and discussion research was not refreshed for this Late edition. The paper uses the fresh board feed and saved public reporting; older posts and local-run claims are not fresh leaderboard results. ARC Raiders closes 13th at 68.75, while ARC Mutants is 62nd at an unchanged 39.31. These are ARC-AGI-2 entries; shared people do not merge their records with teams in ARC-AGI-3."
    }
